--TEST--
A method reference to a `Core` member whose settings object a call must write is refused — `rule:types/callable-values`; the thunk has no literal to flatten and no default to pass instead
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Core\Db::open` takes a `{...}` settings object that has no default. A call
// through a `callable` writes no literal, so nothing could fill it.
callable $open = Core\Db::open(...);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0793]: `Core\Db::open` cannot be used as a method reference
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
